# Toolchain & Project Structure

## Language

**C11** (`-std=c11`), POSIX.1-2008 feature macro `-D_POSIX_C_SOURCE=200809L`. No C++.

## Compiler

**GCC** (preferred) or **Clang**, selected in the `Makefile`. Required flags include `-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Werror`. See `Makefile` comments for rationale.

## Build system

**GNU Make** with the root `Makefile`. Targets: `all` / `yes-toto`, `debug`, `test`, `clean`, `install`.

## Dependencies

**libc only** (no extra `-l`). Headers may include POSIX APIs (`unistd.h`, `signal.h`, …).

## Directory layout (authoritative)

```
yes-toto/
├── .cursor/rules/
├── Makefile
├── README.md
├── include/
│   └── yes_toto.h
├── src/
│   └── main.c
└── tests/
    └── test_core.c
```

- Public prototypes and `fill_buffer()` live in **`include/yes_toto.h`**.
- **`src/main.c`** is the only compilation unit for the `yes-toto` binary (single TU build in `Makefile`).
- **`tests/test_core.c`** compiles alone against the header (inline `fill_buffer`).
